    "answer": {
      "short": "$p=3$, $q=-5$.",
      "worked": "Apply $f$ to both sides of $f^{-1}(18)=g(3)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}18&=f(g(3))\\\\18&=4g(3)+2\\\\g(3)&=4.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $g(4)=7$ and $g(3)=4$,\n$$\\begin{align*}4p+q&=7\\\\3p+q&=4\\\\p&=3.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into $3p+q=4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3(3)+q&=4\\\\q&=-5.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
